## Architecture (2-Stage Summarization)

```
249 Annotated JSONs
    ↓  (05) Merge by topic boundaries
Topical Segments ([TRANSCRIPT] ... [VISUAL] ...)
    ↓  (06) FLAN-T5 pseudo-summary generation
Dataset with Summaries (quality filtered)
    ↓  (07) Tokenize + entity masks + split
Train / Val / Test PyTorch Datasets
    ↓  (08) Fine-tune BART-large-cnn
Trained Summarizer
    ↓  (inference — future scripts 09-11)
Per-segment summaries → concatenate → FLAN-T5 → Full lecture summary
```

---

## How to Execute

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Run all commands from the **project root** directory: `d:\Users\Mihir\Downloads\Documents\Mihir Codes\Dp_Project`

### 0. Install New Dependencies
```bash
pip install rouge-score bert-score accelerate evaluate
```

### 1. Prepare Data (Script 05)
Creates topical segments from your 249 annotated JSONs using topic segmentation boundaries.
```bash
# Test first (3 lectures only)
python scripts/text_processing/05_prepare_bart_data.py --test

# Full run (all 249 lectures)
python scripts/text_processing/05_prepare_bart_data.py
```
**Output**: `data/processed/bart_dataset/prepared_segments.json`

### 2. Generate Pseudo-Summaries (Script 06)
Uses FLAN-T5-base to generate summaries, then filters by quality.
```bash
# Test first (5 segments)
python scripts/text_processing/06_generate_pseudo_summaries.py --test

# Full run
python scripts/text_processing/06_generate_pseudo_summaries.py
```
**Output**: `data/processed/bart_dataset/dataset_with_summaries.json` + `summary_review_samples.json`

> [!WARNING]
> **After this step**: Open `summary_review_samples.json` and skim 20 examples. If summaries look wrong, adjust the prompt in the script before proceeding.

### 3. Create BART Dataset (Script 07)
Tokenizes data, creates entity masks, splits by lecture.
```bash
# Test (10 samples)
python scripts/text_processing/07_create_bart_dataset.py --test

# Full run
python scripts/text_processing/07_create_bart_dataset.py
```
**Output**: `data/processed/bart_dataset/bart_tokenized_dataset.pkl` + `tokenizer/`

### 4. Train BART (Script 08)
Fine-tunes with entity-aware loss, ROUGE evaluation, and early stopping.

```bash
# Test mode (2 training steps, verify it works)
python scripts/text_processing/08_train_bart_summarizer.py --test

# Local 4GB GPU (uses bart-base, smaller model)
python scripts/text_processing/08_train_bart_summarizer.py --small

# Colab / large GPU (uses bart-large-cnn, better quality)
python scripts/text_processing/08_train_bart_summarizer.py
```
**Output**: `models/text/bart_summarizer/best_model/` + `training_history.json`

---

## GPU Recommendations

| Hardware | Command | Notes |
|----------|---------|-------|
| 4GB GPU (local) | `--small` flag | Uses `bart-base` (139M params) |
| Colab T4 (16GB) | No flags needed | Uses `bart-large-cnn` (406M params) |
| CPU only | Add `--small` | Very slow, only for testing |

---

## Troubleshooting

| Issue | Fix |
|-------|-----|
| `CUDA out of memory` | Use `--small` flag, or reduce `batch_size` in config |
| `No segments created` | Check that annotation JSONs exist in `data/annotations/` |
| `segmentation_results.json not found` | Script falls back to chunking — this is OK |
| Low quality scores | Adjust `flan_t5.min_quality_score` in config (lower = accept more) |
| High truncation % | Increase `bart.max_input_length` in config |
